From ab5c40bd0cf68f5288ecb37f14ce51712a5e8c2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:17:27 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Make dynamic registration change a shared tree in place
 (issue 2)

Registration used to return a new tree on every call, so apps had to track
many tree versions. The tree is now a live object:

- registerScreens, registerEdges and registerActions mutate and return the
  same tree. Added items are flagged dynamic.
- setDefaultTree / getDefaultTree / setAsDefault let registration work
  without passing a tree around. The no-tree form no longer builds a
  throwaway empty tree.
- unregisterScreens, unregisterEdges and clearDynamic remove dynamic items.
  File screens and edges cannot be removed.
- createTree makes an empty tree. cloneTree makes an independent copy.
- Registration is staged and committed together, so a failure changes
  nothing. Edge ids are deterministic (no random suffix).
- Adds tests/dynamic.test.ts and updates README, llms.txt, AGENTS.md and
  CHANGELOG.

